  "lineage": "French compositional movement emerging in mid-1970s Paris through the Itinéraire ensemble (founded 1973 by Gérard Grisey, Tristan Murail, Michaël Levinas, and Roger Tessier), generating compositional material from the harmonic-spectrum analysis of acoustic sounds. Grisey's Les Espaces Acoustiques cycle (1974-1985) and Murail's Désintégrations (1982-83) constitute the canonical type-specimens. Distinguished from total serialism by spectralism's acoustic-physical (vs combinatorial-mathematical) compositional logic.",
